# Build
target/
node_modules/
app/dist/
# The public browser demo build (#269) — deployed, never committed
app/dist-demo/

# Vendored sidecar binaries (see sidecars/README.md)
sidecars/*
!sidecars/README.md

# Model weights — never committed. `models/` is a local symlink to wherever
# this machine keeps its weights, so the link itself stays out too.
*.gguf
models

# Run artefacts (per-run directories: inputs hashes, model I/O logs, reports)
runs/

# Local eval results against real data
evals/local/

# Eval recordings and resume state (#293). These live under evals/ so
# `cargo clean` cannot take them — they are hours of measuring, not
# build output — but they are far too large for git: one 355-fixture
# recording is 8.1MB.
#
# `evals/runs/` is named here even though the bare `runs/` rule above
# already catches it. That rule is for the app's per-run directories,
# and tightening it to `/runs/` some day would silently start committing
# recordings. A file this size should be excluded on purpose.
evals/runs/
evals/resume/

# A recording carried off a rented GPU lands here as a tarball before it
# is unpacked and archived (evals/RENTED-GPU.md). Same bytes as the two
# directories above and the same reason to keep them out — named
# separately because they arrive at the repo root, where `git add -A`
# would sweep them into whatever PR was open at the time.
pod-*.tgz

# Somebody's real records must never enter the repo — synthetic fixtures
# only. Name any real document *.private.<ext> and it stays out.
#
# Not just statements: a letter arrives as a photograph, and the OCR'd
# text of one is the same disclosure as the picture (#399). The list
# covers every form a real document reaches this tree in — the file
# chosen, a conversion of it, and the text pulled out of it.
*.private.csv
*.private.pdf
*.private.txt
*.private.md
*.private.jpg
*.private.jpeg
*.private.png
*.private.heic
*.private.heif
# A phone does not name files in lower case. `core.ignorecase` hides
# this on macOS and does not on Linux or in CI, and the failure mode is
# a real letter that was ignored on the machine it was taken on and
# committable everywhere else.
*.private.JPG
*.private.JPEG
*.private.PNG
*.private.HEIC
*.private.HEIF

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Agent worktrees — scratch checkouts, never part of the repo
.claude/worktrees/
.gstack/

# A rented-GPU run's own output (scripts/pod-eval.sh).
#
# Not tidiness: the script refuses a dirty tree, deliberately, because a
# measurement should name a commit. Its own log, baseline, manifest and
# tarball land in the repo — so without this, running it a second time
# refuses on the first run's leftovers, and the fix under time pressure
# is to delete evidence of a run that has not been archived yet.
pod-eval.log
pod-run.out
pod-run.tgz
pod-baseline-*.json
MANIFEST-pod.md
